    "extraction_notes": [
      "PNP datasheet voltages and currents are represented as positive magnitudes in numeric fields; signed PNP test values are preserved in conditions.",
      "The datasheet table gives DC current-gain minimums of 60, 80, 100, 60, and 30 at |IC| = 0.1 mA, 1 mA, 10 mA, 50 mA, and 100 mA respectively, with a maximum of 300 at |IC| = 10 mA; the gain_points target the typical 25 degC curve in fig. 13 rather than guaranteed limits.",
      "The datasheet table gives |VCE(sat)| maximums of 0.25 V at |IC| = 10 mA, |IB| = 1 mA and 0.4 V at |IC| = 50 mA, |IB| = 5 mA. It gives VBE(sat) bounds of 0.65 to 0.85 V at 10 mA/1 mA and a maximum of 0.95 V at 50 mA/5 mA; saturation points use typical 25 degC curves instead of treating limits as typical values.",
      "The fT table value is a guaranteed minimum of 250 MHz at |IC| = 10 mA and |VCE| = 20 V; fig. 18 is a separate typical curve at |VCE| = 2 V and 25 degC.",
      "Cobo and Cibo are maximum capacitance limits, not typical values: 4.5 pF at |VCB| = 5 V and 10 pF at |VEB| = 0.5 V, both at 1 MHz.",
      "Absolute-rating metadata from p. 1 includes |VCEO| = 40 V, |VCBO| = 40 V, |VEBO| = 5 V, continuous |IC| = 0.2 A, peak |ICM| = 0.8 A, and PD = 0.225 W on FR-5 at TA = 25 degC or 0.3 W on alumina at TA = 25 degC.",
      "No output-characteristics IC-versus-VCE figure is provided, so Early voltage VAF cannot be extracted from this datasheet; any F2 model must hold VAF at a family-typical default and mark output conductance as approximate.",
      "The capacitance-versus-reverse-bias figure on p. 3 was not digitized because the single tabulated Cobo and Cibo points are the minimum capacitance inputs needed for an honest F2 attempt.",
      "No temperature-dependent fit was attempted; the curves at -55 degC and 150 degC are not used in the 25 degC extraction."
    ],
    "omission_reason": "VAF is omitted because the datasheet has no output-characteristics figure from which to extract an Early voltage; temperature-dependent parameters, reverse operation, noise, and full transient-curve digitization are also outside this minimum F2 extraction."
  },
